cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "STEWIE: Surface Terrain Engineering & World-model Integration Environment"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: John
    family-names: McCardle
  - given-names: "Aaron W."
    family-names: Storey
repository-code: "https://github.com/stewie-sw/stewie"
url: "https://github.com/stewie-sw/stewie"
abstract: >-
  STEWIE is a digital-twin and mission-planning platform for off-world surface
  construction, built on a mass-conserving terramechanics authority parameterized
  per planetary body (Moon, Mars, Earth, and more). It loads real lunar terrain,
  authors construction goals, produces physically valid and energy-aware plans,
  simulates and renders execution, and emits a mission-control report plus a
  machine-consumable plan. The dynamics are conserved by construction (exact,
  unhackable); learning is spent only on the expensive perception branch. Lineage:
  NASA IPEx (ISRU Pilot Excavator) and the JHU APL Lunar Autonomy Challenge.
keywords:
  - terramechanics
  - lunar robotics
  - regolith
  - in-situ resource utilization
  - mission planning
  - digital twin
  - reinforcement learning
  - Gymnasium
  - world model
  - NASA IPEx
  - Lunar Autonomy Challenge
version: 0.1.0
